  data:  # b8c9
    kind: invariant  # b8c9
    title: "Sanitizer registration read the NAME slot for receiver evidence that production puts in the MODULE slot — INV-finoh's permit branch was unreachable, and the ADR-0017 barrier arm was dead at every idiomatic call site"  # b8c9
    status: satisfied  # b8c9
    priority: 2  # b8c9
    parent:  # b8c9
    tags:  # b8c9
    - taint  # b8c9
    - adr_0017  # b8c9
    - analysis_quality  # b8c9
    - awaits_bakeoff_validation  # b8c9
    isbefore: []  # b8c9
    duplicate_of: []  # b8c9
    not_duplicate_of: []  # b8c9
    pr_ref: 8b1a20cc1b  # b8c9
    description: "INSTANCE OF THE RECEIVER-EVIDENCE CLASS, on the SANITIZER role. Sibling of\nINV-linub rather than a child: the evidence is PRESENT here and read from the\nwrong slot, where INV-linub is about the evidence being ABSENT.\n\nWHAT IS WRONG. _register_sanitizer_callers refuses an unresolved edge carrying\nmeta.call_construct == \"method\" unless the callee is qualified. That gate is\nINV-finoh's and is correct in purpose -- binding a bare x.encrypt() to\nFernet.encrypt would falsely sanitize a real flow, a false NEGATIVE, the\nexpensive direction for a security tool.\n\nThe permit branch was:\n\n    qualified = any(s.qualified_name == callee_name for s in matched_list)\n\nwhere callee_name = _extract_callee_name(edge[\"dst\"]) -- the NAME SLOT.\nProduction analyzers put an inferred receiver type in the MODULE SLOT:\n\n    py:external:0-0:Fernet.encrypt:unresolved      <- synthetic, tests only\n    py:cryptography.fernet.Fernet:0-0:encrypt:...  <- what analyzers emit\n\nSo the comparison was \"cryptography.fernet.Fernet.encrypt\" == \"encrypt\",\nFALSE BY CONSTRUCTION for any method-shaped sanitizer. Every sanitizer in the\nshipped catalogue is method-shaped (Fernet.encrypt, AESGCM.encrypt,\nAESCCM.encrypt, ChaCha20Poly1305.encrypt, AEAD.Seal, Cipher.doFinal). The\nrefusal was therefore UNCONDITIONAL in production and the ADR-0017 sanitizer\nbarrier arm was dead at every idiomatic call site.\n\nThis is a default-deny whose permitting case cannot fire -- the failure mode\nthe decision rule in the lab notebook names (\"enumerate the PERMITTING case\")\n-- and a name-slot/module-slot near-miss twin.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL REPRO (live, shipped catalogue, no --taint-* overrides):\n\n  probeB/h.py:\n      import os\n      from cryptography.fernet import Fernet\n\n      def handler(f: Fernet, token):\n          plain = f.decrypt(token)\n          safe = f.encrypt(plain)\n          os.remove(safe)\n\n  hypergumbo verify-claims probeB --claims plaintext.claims.yaml --json\n\n  BEFORE: verdict \"violated\", confidence \"precise\", sanitized_flows 0,\n          evidence Fernet.decrypt -> os.remove. A false positive about code\n          that visibly encrypts.\n  AFTER:  verdict \"confirmed\", sanitized_flows 1, barrier arm fires\n          (barrier_lines=frozenset({7}) -> False).\n\nInstrumented at the gate, the two probe forms emit a BYTE-IDENTICAL dst\n(python:cryptography.fernet.Fernet:0-0:encrypt:external_symbol) and differ\nonly in meta.call_construct (None vs \"method\"); that alone flipped\nsanitizer_lines from {(handler,'plaintext'): [7,7,7,7]} to {}. Both printed\nqualified-match? False -- the permit branch never fired in either.\n\nFIX. Consult the module slot via _module_from_symbol_path, which returns \"\"\nfor the \"external\" placeholder BY DOCUMENTED DESIGN -- so an untyped receiver\nstill yields no candidate and is still refused. INV-finoh's guarantee is\nPRESERVED, not widened. The WHOLE qualified name must match: a typed receiver\nof the WRONG type is evidence AGAINST this sanitizer, pinned by its own test\n(AESGCM.encrypt must not satisfy a registered Fernet.encrypt).\n\nDIRECTION -- SUPPRESSIVE, and measured before shipping. More sanitizers\nregister -> more barrier walks -> more False -> more sanitized, and since\nPR #214 a False DROPS the flow from the violation set.\nInstrument: scripts/measure-sanitizer-module-slot-ab.py (in-repo). It disables\nthe module slot ONLY inside sanitizer registration, so source/sink matching is\nuntouched and the A/B measures the change under test rather than a superset.\nPredictions pre-registered before any number was read (S5-PREREGISTRATION.md);\nall four held.\n\n  repo         gate reached A/B   sanitizer sites A/B   evidence A/B\n  pretix       1 / 1              0 / 0                 0 / 0    REFUSAL\n  hypergumbo   0 / 0              0 / 0                 0 / 0    ABSENCE\n  kserve       0 / 0              0 / 0                 0 / 0    ABSENCE\n  caddy        0 / 0              0 / 0                 2 / 2    ABSENCE\n\nCORPUS DELTA ZERO IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. The load-bearing row is pretix -- the\ncorpus's ONLY edge that reaches the gate (the bare `encrypt` WI-fasub found).\nIt stays REFUSED in both arms: live evidence that an untyped receiver still\ncannot sanitize. Positive control differed as required (+4 call sites,\n+1 barrier walk), so the corpus zeros are controlled nulls rather than an\ninstrument that cannot see.\n\nREACH LIMIT, stated rather than left implicit. The module slot reaches taint\nonly for python (taint_refine's annotation pinning, gated lang == \"python\" at\ncli.py) and java (PR #227's analyzer emit). Go, rust and typescript sanitizers\ncannot present a module slot at all today, so this buys them nothing until\ntheir analyzers emit one. Python's own coverage is limited to ANNOTATED\nreceivers; the unannotated `f = Fernet(key); f.encrypt(x)` still carries the\nexternal placeholder and still needs WI-zilag.\n\nWHY THIS IS NOT INV-finoh REOPENED. INV-finoh's statement is that a phantom\nbarrier must not register; that still holds and is still tested. This defect\nis the opposite error -- over-refusal of a barrier whose receiver evidence was\npresent. INV-finoh's closure evidence used propagate_taint_structural with\nsynthetic name-slot edges, which is why a satisfied item shipped an\nunreachable permit branch; that is a closure-evidence gap on a correct fix,\nrecorded on its thread."  # b8c9
    fields:  # b8c9
      statement: "Sanitizer registration MUST recognise receiver evidence in whichever slot of the dst symbol id it occupies. Production analyzers put an inferred receiver type in the MODULE slot; a permit branch that consults only the NAME slot can never fire for a method-shaped sanitizer, and every shipped sanitizer is method-shaped."  # b8c9
      root_cause: "taint.py _register_sanitizer_callers compared TaintSanitizer.qualified_name against _extract_callee_name(edge['dst']), which returns the name slot only. For python:cryptography.fernet.Fernet:0-0:encrypt:external_symbol that is 'encrypt', never 'cryptography.fernet.Fernet.encrypt', so the qualified-callee escape hatch on the INV-finoh call_construct=='method' refusal was unreachable in production."  # b8c9
