  message: "CLOSURE RATIONALE. Fixed in dev 8b1a20cc1b. Satisfied on BEHAVIOURAL evidence\non the production path (verify-claims -> propagate_taint_ddg), not a proxy:\nthe idiomatic probe (def handler(f: Fernet): plain = f.decrypt(token); safe =\nf.encrypt(plain); os.remove(safe)) went verdict \"violated\"/precise/\nsanitized_flows=0 -> \"confirmed\"/sanitized_flows=1, with the barrier arm\nobserved firing (barrier_lines=frozenset({7}) -> False) under a wrapper on\n_ddg_taint_reaches. Shipped catalogue, no --taint-* overrides.\n\nNON-DESTRUCTION, on live data rather than only in a unit test: pretix is the\ncorpus's ONLY edge that reaches this gate (a bare `encrypt`, the one WI-fasub\nfound) and it stays REFUSED in both arms -- an untyped receiver still carries\nthe `external` placeholder, still yields no module, still cannot sanitize.\nINV-finoh's guarantee is preserved, not widened. A second test pins that a\ntyped receiver of the WRONG type (AESGCM.encrypt vs a registered\nFernet.encrypt) does not sanitize; it passed BEFORE the change and must stay\ngreen, so it is a guard rather than a regression test.\n\nTAG NOTE. awaits_bakeoff_validation is attached, but the quantitative claim\nbeing validated is a measured ZERO (corpus delta 0 in both directions across\npretix/hypergumbo/kserve/caddy). The queue entry exists to catch that delta\nbecoming NON-zero as receiver typing lands -- it is not awaiting confirmation\nof an improvement."  # ea91
